<div class="blurb">
<div class="header"><h2>validated claims</h2></div>
<div class="body">
<p>The following claims have been validated with 4 independent sources each:</p>

<h3>Claim 1: Fast Food Restaurants Use MSG</h3>
<ul>
<li>KFC uses MSG in many food items including Original Recipe chicken <sup><a href="#src-qsr-1">109</a></sup></li>
<li>Burger King uses MSG in some processed products <sup><a href="#src-qsr-2">110</a></sup></li>
<li>Chick-fil-A confirms MSG in some menu items <sup><a href="#src-qsr-3">111</a>, <a href="#src-qsr-4">112</a></sup></li>
</ul>

<h3>Claim 2: MSG is FDA GRAS</h3>
<ul>
<li>FDA considers MSG "Generally Recognized As Safe" (GRAS) <sup><a href="#src-fda">73</a>, <a href="#src-fda-2">74</a></sup></li>
<li>University of Illinois dietitians confirm no scientific evidence MSG is harmful <sup><a href="#src-ui">113</a></sup></li>
<li>Peer-reviewed studies support MSG safety at normal consumption levels <sup><a href="#src-fda-3">75</a>, <a href="#src-fda-4">76</a>, <a href="#src-fda">73</a>, <a href="#src-fda-2">74</a></sup></li>
</ul>

<h3>Claim 3: MSG Can Cause Adverse Reactions</h3>
<ul>
<li>Some individuals report headaches after consuming MSG <sup><a href="#src-headache">19</a>, <a href="#src-headache-2">20</a></sup></li>
<li>Systematic reviews show mixed evidence requiring more research <sup><a href="#src-headache-3">21</a>, <a href="#src-headache-4">22</a></sup></li>
<li>Current Pain and Headache Reports calls for continued investigation <sup><a href="#src-headache-4">22</a></sup></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
